  era: "Section 35 \xB7 Religion in India \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Zoroastrianism
  text: Zoroastrians from Persia settled in Gujarat around the 8th to 10th centuries, becoming the Parsis. Though few in number, Parsis have shaped modern India; they include Dadabhai Naoroji and the Tata family.
